// A map literal keyed by a type with no runtime key form — here a user struct, even a
// derived-`Comparable` one — is rejected statically (the runtime accepts only strings and
// key-capable extern types; structural object keys do not exist yet). Previously this
// type-checked and failed at the first insertion.
// expect: error E0007 at 10:5
// expect: exit 1
@derive(Comparable, Equatable)
struct P { x: int }

m = { P { x: 1 }: "one" }
echo m.len()
